Passage: REG, Annex III, 1.3.8.2

[0] 1.3.8.2.
[1] Moving parts involved in the process Guards or protective devices designed to protect persons against the hazards generated by moving parts involved in the process shall be:
[2] (a) either fixed guards as referred to in section 1.4.2.1;
[3] or (b) interlocking movable guards as referred to in section 1.4.2.2;
[4] or (c) protective devices as referred to in section 1.4.3;
[5] or (d) a combination of the above.
[6] However, when certain moving parts directly involved in the process cannot be made completely inaccessible during operation owing to operations requiring operator intervention, such parts shall be fitted with:
[7] (a) fixed guards or interlocking movable guards preventing access to those sections of the parts that are not used in the work;
[8] and (b) adjustable guards as referred to in section 1.4.2.3 restricting access to those sections of the moving parts where access is necessary.
